            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allergies have become more widespread on the medical landscape of developed countries over recent years. Left untreated, or poorly treated, they are responsible for a high level of morbidity and underestimated social prejudice. Screening, treatment and monitoring are essential.</AbstractText>
